A note on what this covers, because it is easy to get wrong:

This licence covers agent-browser itself. It depends on Playwright, the Model Context Protocol SDK
and Zod, each licensed separately by its own authors under its own terms, and Playwright downloads
browser builds from Microsoft under theirs. None of that is affected by this licence.

The software drives a real web browser and acts on real websites on your behalf. You are
responsible for what you point it at: the terms of the sites you visit, the accounts you sign into,
and the credentials you make available to it. It reports a bot challenge or a block page rather
than trying to get around one, and that is deliberate.
